    <h1>The weekend, meals, and what to bring</h1>
    <p class="retreat-comp__lede">Everything below is included in your registration. Check-in opens Friday at 4pm, and we're out by 10am Sunday.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="retreat-section retreat-details" id="schedule">
  <div class="retreat-section__inner">
    <h2>The shape of the weekend</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Friday</strong></li>
      <li>4:00pm · Arrive and settle in, snacks set out. The gate doesn't open to us until 4:00, so please don't arrive early.</li>
      <li>6:00pm · Dinner</li>
      <li>7:15pm · Evening session: introductions, a talk, conversation and songs</li>
      <li>9:50pm · Fire</li>
      <li><strong>Saturday</strong></li>
      <li>6:30am · Morning workout (optional)</li>
      <li>7:30am · Coffee</li>
      <li>8:00–10:00am · Breakfast</li>
      <li>10:00am · Morning session: short talks, whole-room discussion and small groups, with a break midway</li>
      <li>Around 1:00pm · Lunch</li>
      <li>2:00pm · Free time: trails, boats, disc golf, or rest</li>
      <li>4:00pm · Afternoon session: short talks, whole-room discussion and small groups, with a break midway</li>
      <li>Around 6:45pm · Dinner</li>
      <li>8:00pm · Fireside, until about 10</li>
      <li><strong>Sunday</strong></li>
      <li>7:00am · Coffee and breakfast; strip your bed</li>
      <li>8:30am · Meditation, then a closing check-in</li>
      <li>9:25am · Clean up together; out by 10</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="retreat-section retreat-details" id="meals">
  <div class="retreat-section__inner">
    <h2>Meals</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Friday dinner, 6:00pm · taco bar</strong> from Linita's Catering in Nunnelly: chicken and beef, tortillas and chips, queso and nacho cheese, shredded cheese, lettuce, tomato, onions, jalapeños, sour cream, salsa, rice and refried beans. Tea and lemonade.</li>
      <li><strong>Saturday breakfast, 8:00–10:00am · breakfast bar</strong> from Linita's: bacon and sausage patties, eggs, and breakfast sides.</li>
      <li><strong>Saturday lunch, around 1:00pm · loaded baked potato bar</strong> from Linita's: baked potatoes with butter, cheese, cheese sauce, bacon, pulled pork, chicken, chives, sour cream, barbecue sauce and ranch. Tea and lemonade.</li>
      <li><strong>Saturday dinner, around 6:45pm · Southern dinner</strong> from Purdie's Catering: maple mustard glazed chicken and pot roast with gravy; smashed potatoes, green beans with bacon, and balsamic grilled vegetables; rolls; berry cream pie and a second dessert. Tea.</li>
      <li><strong>Sunday breakfast, 7:00–8:30am:</strong> a light continental breakfast</li>
      <li><strong>All weekend:</strong> coffee, tea and light snacks</li>
      <li><strong>Dietary needs:</strong> we've passed along the dietary needs you gave us to the caterers. If you have a serious allergy, or anything has changed, email <a href="mailto:admin@christiantranshumanism.org?subject=CTA%20Retreat%20dietary%20needs">admin@christiantranshumanism.org</a> so we can confirm it with them directly.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="retreat-section retreat-details" id="bring">
  <div class="retreat-section__inner">
    <h2>What to bring</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Bedding and towels are provided</strong> in the lodge. No need to pack sheets or a sleeping bag.</li>
      <li><strong>Clothes in layers:</strong> mid-October evenings in the Tennessee hills get cool, and we'll be by the fire in the evenings, weather permitting.</li>
      <li><strong>Shoes for the outdoors:</strong> sturdy shoes for the trails and the gravel paths. A rain jacket, in case.</li>
      <li><strong>Toiletries</strong> and any medications you need for the weekend.</li>
      <li><strong>A water bottle</strong> and a phone charger.</li>
      <li><strong>Something to write on,</strong> if you want it.</li>
      <li><strong>Instruments and games:</strong> bring an instrument if you play, since there's music by the fire. Card and board games are welcome too.</li>
      <li><strong>Your own extra snacks and drinks:</strong> we'll have the meals above, plus coffee, tea and light snacks. For anything else you can't do without (a Diet Coke habit, say), bring your own supply. :)</li>
      <li><strong>Please leave at home:</strong> alcohol and tobacco. Woodlands is an alcohol- and tobacco-free property.</li>
      <li><strong>Getting in:</strong> the gate code and directions will come to registrants by email before the weekend.</li>
      <li><strong>Questions:</strong> <a href="mailto:admin@christiantranshumanism.org?subject=CTA%20Retreat">admin@christiantranshumanism.org</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

